                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The art and overall idea is great, I will admit ([spoiler]beginning of the existence tied to a noir detective case[/spoiler]). \r\n\r\nHowever, this alone didn't \"hook\" me like other \"artful\" games, which left the gameplay, music, and \"plot\" to pick up the slack. \r\n\r\nSadly, the gameplay, though varied from what I saw, was not engaging, just busy work to progress; the music was \"noir,\" but did not stand out; and the \"plot\" did not grab me either, as much as I understood what was going on.\r\n\r\nI did not finish it. It was not terrible, but I wasn't getting anything from the experience. I wouldn't go out of my way to recommend this to anyone unless the art style really really appeals.",
